The files in this directory come from three sources.

1. Galagino by Till Harbaum (https://github.com/harbaum/galagino, main at
   commit cdd21cdf6e1b), published under the GNU General Public License v3.0
   (galagino.ino: "Published under GPLv3"):

     i8048.c, i8048.h            the Intel 8048 core of the Donkey Kong sound
                                 CPU, derived by Galagino from asig/kosmos-cp1
                                 (GPL-3.0); changed for this port: true/false,
                                 the ROM pointer and a cycle counter, see the
                                 note in i8048.h
     tileaddr.h, dip_switches.h  unchanged
     data/*_logo.h               the game menu logos, unchanged
     data/galaga_starseed.h      the Galaga star sets, unchanged
     data/galaga_sample_boom.h   the Galaga explosion sample, unchanged
     data/dkong_sample_*.h       the Donkey Kong walk, jump and stomp samples,
                                 unchanged

   and, ported to C for this project from Galagino's pacman.h, galaga.h,
   dkong.h, frogger.h, digdug.h, 1942.h, emulation.c, galagino.ino and the
   romconv/*.py converters:

     game_pacman.c, game_galaga.c, game_dkong.c, game_frogger.c,
     game_digdug.c, game_1942.c, gal_gfx.c, gal_sound.c, gal_menu.c

2. The MAME project (https://github.com/mamedev/mame), under the BSD-3-Clause
   licence below, taken from pico-mooncresta (MAME master at commit
   1ecdb5701405):

     z80.c, z80.h                src/devices/cpu/z80/z80.cpp, z80.h, z80.inc
                                 Juergen Buchmueller; one addition for this
                                 port, z80_hold_irq() (MAME's HOLD_LINE)
     z80.lst                     src/devices/cpu/z80/z80.lst, unchanged
                                 Juergen Buchmueller, Andrei I. Holub
     z80_ops.h                   generated from z80.lst by tools/z80gen.py,
                                 which is derived from src/devices/cpu/z80/
                                 z80make.py: Andre I. Holub

   Timing and interrupt details of the games follow MAME's drivers
   (src/mame/namco/galaga.cpp, src/mame/galaxian/galaxian.cpp).

3. Original to pico-galagino, under the GNU General Public License v3.0 with
   the rest of the project:

     galagino.h, gal_internal.h, gal_core.c, gal_games.c, gal_flash.c,
     gal_port.h, romload.c, romload.h (romload.c generalised from
     pico-mooncresta)

